erence-route state join; planar relation to coarse masked OSW display polygons.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"state_evidence\": [],\n      \"connections\": [],\n      \"scope_notes\": [\n        {\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-equatorial-undercurrent\",\n          \"label\": \"Dated subsurface band and transient undercurrent definition\",\n          \"audit_file\": \"research/indian-euc-dated-band-layer-season-scope-audit.json\",\n          \"summary\": \"The 1–3 March 2017 section at 90 E describes a roughly 300 km meridional current/salinity band span in the 80–150 m depth range. This is a local descriptive metric, not full width at every depth or along the current. Historical longitudinal samples do not establish one simultaneous axis; overlying flow, transient structure and seasonal exceptions need separate review.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://repository.library.noaa.gov/view/noaa/64055/noaa_64055_DS1.pdf\",\n          \"source_locator\": \"Data and Methods p. 3; Results p. 4 and Conclusions p. 5. Historical interpretation: Schott/McCreary (2001), sections 3.2–3.2.2, printed pp. 28–31.\",\n          \"observed_period\": {\n            \"start\": \"2017-03-01\",\n            \"end\": \"2017-03-03\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"evidence_links\": [],\n      \"object_url\": \"object.html?id=current%3Aindian-equatorial-undercurrent\",\n      \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\n      \"season_url\": \"seasons.html?current=indian-equatorial-undercurrent\",\n      \"dashboard_search\": \"Indian Ocean Equatorial Undercurrent Equatorial Indian Ocean\",\n      \"width_ids\": [\n        \"indian-euc-2017-03-described-subsurface-band\"\n      ],\n      \"measurement_ids\": [],\n      \"route_ids\": [\n        \"indian-euc-spring-observation-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"source:0a9db1d0e73f03d0\",\n        \"source:4dc5fc618c265