to coarse masked OSW display polygons.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"state_evidence\": [],\n      \"connections\": [],\n      \"scope_notes\": [\n        {\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent\",\n          \"label\": \"Northern Tsuchiya mean cores and integration limits\",\n          \"audit_file\": \"research/pacific-nscc-reach-layer-section-scope-audit.json\",\n          \"summary\": \"155 W to 110 W is an editorial northern Tsuchiya studied reach. Local mean cores shoal from 220 m to 130 m; no uniform axis depth inferred. Transport integration latitude limits are not width. Historical compilation dates do not date the route, and the 130 E NEUC identity is kept separate. A separate Rowe et al. general 2-degree meridional width summary is now retained as approximately 220 km; the two jet records share one source claim, not independent observations or annual extrema.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www.pmel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml\",\n          \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2-3 and Table 1: north SSCC peaks at 155 W 3.5 N/220 m and 110 W 4.5 N/130 m. Transport integration latitude limits and 700-dbar reference are separately defined; they are not route width or a uniform axis layer.\",\n          \"observed_period\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"evidence_links\": [],\n      \"object_url\": \"object.html?id=current%3Apacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent\",\n      \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\n      \"season_url\": \"seasons.html?current=pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent\",\n      \"dashboard_search\": \"Pacific North Subsurface Countercurrent Equatorial North Pacific\",\n      \"width_ids\": [\n        \"pacific-north-subsurface-countercurrent-rowe-2000-general-angular-width\"\n      ],\n      \"measurement_ids\": [],\n      \"route_ids\": [\n        \"pacific-nscc-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": 