mel.noaa.gov/pubs/outstand/john1806/john1806.shtml\",\n          \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2-3 and Table 1: south SSCC peaks at 155 W 3.5 S/250 m and 110 W 5.5 S/160 m. Latitude integration bands are not widths. Rowe et al. (2000), introduction and section 3e/Fig. 10 caption, distinguish primary and secondary southern jets.\",\n          \"observed_period\": null\n        }\n      ],\n      \"evidence_links\": [],\n      \"object_url\": \"object.html?id=current%3Apacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent\",\n      \"route_url\": \"reference-routes.html#pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\n      \"season_url\": \"seasons.html?current=pacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent\",\n      \"dashboard_search\": \"Pacific South Subsurface Countercurrent Equatorial South Pacific\",\n      \"width_ids\": [\n        \"pacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent-rowe-2000-general-angular-width\"\n      ],\n      \"measurement_ids\": [],\n      \"route_ids\": [\n        \"pacific-sscc-mean-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"source:4dc5fc618c26565f\",\n        \"source:4f7441b953be4651\",\n        \"source:803229fe82eb2360\",\n        \"source:b038491b0e5a3967\",\n        \"source:df8a86f107aba236\"\n      ],\n      \"state_codes\": [],\n      \"published_length_km\": null,\n      \"width_sample_ids\": [],\n      \"route_decision_ids\": [\n        \"route-decision:pacific-south-subsurface-countercurrent\"\n      ],\n      \"current_section_ids\": [],\n      \"velocity_sample_ids\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"current:persian-gulf-saline-overflow\",\n      \"label\": \"Persian Gulf saline overflow\",\n      \"type\": \"named_current\",\n      \"identity_level\": \"current\",\n      \"source_kind\": \"dense saline strait overflow\",\n      \"setting\": \"regional\",\n      \"time_behavior\": \"persistent_variable\",\n      \"basin\": \"Persian Gulf / Gulf of Oman\",\n      \"capabilities\": {\n        \"observed_veloc