on to coarse masked OSW display polygons.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"state_evidence\": [],\n      \"connections\": [],\n      \"scope_notes\": [\n        {\n          \"current_id\": \"red-sea-saline-overflow\",\n          \"label\": \"Winter plume reach and channel branch taxonomy\",\n          \"audit_file\": \"research/red-sea-redsox-branch-reach-scope-audit.json\",\n          \"summary\": \"A source-reported winter Northern Channel plume reach is about 130 km with speed above 0.2 m/s. Channel dimensions use different conventions and remain separate from current length/width. Descending branches and downstream equilibrated water need distinct identities; no whole-current or annual dimensions inferred.\",\n          \"source_url\": \"https://www2.whoi.edu/site/bower-lab/wp-content/uploads/sites/12/2018/03/Peters_2005_MixingEntrainment.pdf\",\n          \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2, 3a and 5a; Figure 4 caption.\",\n          \"observed_period\": null,\n          \"supporting_sources\": [\n            {\n              \"label\": \"Equilibration and branch products: Bower et al. (2005)\",\n              \"url\": \"https://www2.whoi.edu/site/bower-lab/wp-content/uploads/sites/12/2018/03/Bower_etal_2005_EquilibrationCirculation.pdf\",\n              \"locator\": \"Sections 2, 3a-b; Table 1; abstract\",\n              \"access\": \"Relevant full-text passages inspected; no raw axes or paired current boundaries extracted.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"evidence_links\": [\n        {\n          \"label\": \"Why the 2003 channel width is not a measured current width\",\n          \"url\": \"query.html?source-q=%7B%22document%22%3A%22research%2Fozgokmen-2003-red-sea-width-scope-review.json%22%2C%22pointer%22%3A%22%2Ffindings%22%2C%22limit%22%3A4%2C%22offset%22%3A0%7D#source-query-title\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"label\": \"Inspect the original-study acquisition receipt\",\n          \"url\": \"query.html?source-q=%7B%22docume