ce equatorial jets. No whole-current length.\",\"seasonal_playback_eligible\":false,\"source_file\":\"research/pacific-secc-western-mean-reference-path-v2-candidate.json\",\"source_file_sha256\":\"a8bb517551f04dbe1018a6d5a51817cee4c3e3afaf2d82447bccdab03cef1d85\",\"source_id\":\"source:chen-qiu-secc-seasonal-2004\",\"source_ids\":[\"source:chen-qiu-secc-seasonal-2004\",\"source:pacific-secc-western-reference-method-v1\"],\"source_locator\":\"Paragraph2 on PDF page1 and Figure1b/caption on PDF page2: western SECC context and mean0-200m geostrophy relative to1500dbar. Selected page2 pixels actually reviewed on2026-10-27.\",\"source_pointer\":\"\",\"source_url\":\"https://www.soest.hawaii.edu/oceanography/bo/CQ04.pdf\",\"status\":\"reviewed_editorial_regional_reference_connection\",\"time_convention\":\"WOA01 mean-field context only. Publication2004 is not an observation date. No dated trajectory or seasonal route reconstructed.\",\"type\":\"editorial_regional_reference_connection\",\"uncertainty_km\":null,\"whole_current_length_km\":null}","source_index_audit":{"added_source_paths":["research/pacific-secc-parent-audit-result-v1.json","research/pacific-secc-parent-audit-selected-records-v1.json","research/pacific-secc-reference-geography-result-v1.json","research/pacific-secc-reference-geography-review-v1.json","research/pacific-secc-reference-publication-admission-v1.json","research/pacific-secc-reference-query-contract-v1.json","research/pacific-secc-reference-runtime-contract-v1.json","research/pacific-secc-western-mean-reference-path-v2-candidate.json"],"original_source_strings_preserved":608,"original_sources_verified":609,"replaced_source_paths":["research/ocean-motion-dashboard.json"],"scientific_source_documents_replaced":0}},"scope":"State joins retain relation kinds; gateways are not containment. Widths retain scope. Published lengths and editorial route lengths are separate collections.","seasons_receipts":{"directions":{"source_file":"research/new-guinea-coastal-current-seasonal-direction-scope-audit.json","source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-seasonal-direction-scope-audit.v1\",\r\n  \"current_id\": \"new-guinea-coastal-current\",\r\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_source_summary_not_canonical\",\r\n  \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242\",\r\n  \"source_citation\": \"Zhang et al. (2020), Seasonal and Interannual Variability of the Currents off the New Guinea Coast From Mooring Measurements, doi:10.1029/2020JC016242.\",\r\n  \"source_access\": \"Publisher abstract, Introduction, Data and Method, sections 3.1–3.3 and figure captions read. No figure, velocity field or axis digitized.\",\r\n  \"observed_period\": {\r\n    \"start\": \"2015-11\",\r\n    \"end\": \"2018-12\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"time_precision\": \"month\",\r\n  \"scope\": \"Local alongshore direction at the 141.4 E, 1.7 S mooring; monthly composite of three cycles, with interannual contamination and instrument gaps. Not a whole-current monthly path.\",\r\n  \"sampling_note\": \"Data above 30 m removed; upper-400 m instrument outage July 2016–March 2017. Monthly averages; three cycles provide limited independence.\",\r\n  \"interpretation\": \"November–April southeastward and May–October northwestward describe the short-record composite. In the 2015/2016 El Niño interval the eastward NGCC disappears as NGCUC shoals. Exception is selectable separately and excluded from seasonal playback.\",\r\n  \"whole_current_length_km\": null,\r\n  \"whole_current_width_km\": null,\r\n  \"annual_length_range_km\": null,\r\n  \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n  \"route_construction_status\": \"not_constructed\",\r\n  \"phases\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"new-guinea-coastal-current\",\r\n      \"geometry_role\": \"local_direction_symbol_not_current_axis\",\r\n      \"site_lon_lat\": [\r\n        141.4,\r\n        -1.7\r\n      ],\r\n      \"layer\": \"Upper-100 m NGCC context; ADCP measurements above 30 m excluded. No uniform layer assigned along a route.\",\r\n      \"length_km\": null,\r\n      \"width_km\": null,\r\n      \"route_coordinates\": null,\r\n      \"annual_length_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242\",\r\n      \"id\": \"ngcc-november-april\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"November–April · three-cycle composite\",\r\n      \"flow_direction\": \"southeastward\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        11,\r\n        12,\r\n        1,\r\n        2,\r\n        3,\r\n        4\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"seasonal_direction_composite\",\r\n      \"playback_eligible\": true,\r\n      \"observed_period\": {\r\n        \"start\": \"2015-11\",\r\n        \"end\": \"2018-12\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 3.2 / Figure 4 caption\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"new-guinea-coastal-current\",\r\n      \"geometry_role\": \"local_direction_symbol_not_current_axis\",\r\n      \"site_lon_lat\": [\r\n        141.4,\r\n        -1.7\r\n      ],\r\n      \"layer\": \"Upper-100 m NGCC context; ADCP measurements above 30 m excluded. No uniform layer assigned along a route.\",\r\n      \"length_km\": null,\r\n      \"width_km\": null,\r\n      \"route_coordinates\": null,\r\n      \"annual_length_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242\",\r\n      \"id\": \"ngcc-may-october\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"May–October · three-cycle composite\",\r\n      \"flow_direction\": \"northwestward\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        5,\r\n        6,\r\n        7,\r\n        8,\r\n        9,\r\n        10\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"seasonal_direction_composite\",\r\n      \"playback_eligible\": true,\r\n      \"observed_period\": {\r\n        \"start\": \"2015-11\",\r\n        \"end\": \"2018-12\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 3.2 / Figure 4 caption\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"new-guinea-coastal-current\",\r\n      \"geometry_role\": \"local_direction_symbol_not_current_axis\",\r\n      \"site_lon_lat\": [\r\n        141.4,\r\n        -1.7\r\n      ],\r\n      \"layer\": \"Upper-100 m NGCC context; ADCP measurements above 30 m excluded. No uniform layer assigned along a route.\",\r\n      \"length_km\": null,\r\n      \"width_km\": null,\r\n      \"route_coordinates\": null,\r\n      \"annual_length_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2020JC016242\",\r\n      \"id\": \"ngcc-el-nino-2015-2016\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"2015/2016 El Niño exception\",\r\n      \"flow_direction\": \"southeastward NGCC absent; northwestward undercurrent shoals\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"event_exception\",\r\n      \"playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"observed_period\": {\r\n        \"start\": \"2015-11\",\r\n        \"end\": \"2016-06\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 3.3 / Figure 9 caption\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n    \"Recover cross-flow boundaries and alongshore axes before seasonal dimensions.\",\r\n    \"Resolve calendar dependence across ENSO states and a longer record.\",\r\n    \"Keep NGCC, NGCUC and newly named intermediate flow distinct.\"\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"8b5fc2d62a5a7c777b69106aa7875260d52bbdff9a2059fbe06d6a1d364652fc"},"frames":{"source_file":"research/ocean-current-seasonal-route-frames.json","source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-seasonal-route-frames.v1\",\r\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-10-04\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_seasonal_route_associations_not_canonical\",\r\n  \"coverage\": \"Somali seasonal components, historical Davidson winter reach, Sri Lanka Monsoon Current summer/winter regional drawings, and one Indian SECC winter surface reach. Incomplete annual coverage; not observed monthly fields or occupied footprints.\",\r\n  \"counts\": {\r\n    \"currents\": 4,\r\n    \"frames\": 6\r\n  },\r\n  \"frames\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"somali-winter\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"somali\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"Northeast winter monsoon\",\r\n      \"flow_direction\": \"southward\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Northeast winter monsoon convention; not a simultaneous dated observation or an annual-average route.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Surface/upper-layer seasonal coastal reference geography; the source describes a shallow winter equatorial current, but no fixed-depth velocity axis is reconstructed.\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_file\": \"research/somali-winter-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_sha256\": \"37cf752d61cfcfff451e3066e842e00f524b78400573b28ff731cf3ff12f4cda\",\r\n      \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n      \"width_measurement_ids\": [],\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 4.2.1, printed pages 48-49 (PDF indices 47-48): southward surface flow reaches EACC confluence at 2-4 S; winter coastal divergence near 6-8 N. Section 4.2.2 distinguishes modeled coastal continuation and northern countercurrent.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"somali-summer-southern\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"somali\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"June-July southern limb\",\r\n      \"flow_direction\": \"northward\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        6,\r\n        7\r\n      ],\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"June-July monsoon-onset two-gyre convention. Does not assume rare late-summer gyre coalescence or persistent whole-coast continuity.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Upper-layer southern seasonal coastal geography; no fixed-depth or velocity-derived axis.\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_file\": \"research/somali-summer-southern-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_sha256\": \"73efa37ee93f5a6985c891bb524fc2ec0d443d17807de420fc7a03a44ab5b295\",\r\n      \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n      \"width_measurement_ids\": [],\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 4.1.1, printed page 38 (PDF index 37): June-July cross-equatorial limb departs the coast south of 4 N, partitions into offshore outflow/recirculation and has little exchange with Great Whirl. Printed pages 41-43 discuss non-universal gyre coalescence.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"davidson-historical-winter\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"davidson\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"October-March (1978 regional summary)\",\r\n      \"flow_direction\": \"northward\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        10,\r\n        11,\r\n        12,\r\n        1,\r\n        2,\r\n        3\r\n      ],\r\n      \"route_candidate_file\": \"research/davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_sha256\": \"ac2db281859e27e8903fb224f3fdde35b36f010ab111240e2a2c78e3c5a26609\",\r\n      \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n      \"width_measurement_ids\": [\r\n        \"davidson-historical-winter-width\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"width_support_role\": \"regional_source_context_not_uniform_route_width\",\r\n      \"width_scope_note\": \"Approximate 64 km is historical California-Oregon regional context; it is not applied uniformly to the editorial route or used as an occupied footprint.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"October-March California-Oregon regional seasonal description in the February 1978 report; strongest flow described in January. Historical summary, not a dated trajectory, current-year observation or modern monthly climatology.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Seasonal northward surface-current regional context; not the separately described California Undercurrent below 200 m or a reconstructed velocity axis.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/40591190_v2.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Appendix II section II.1, printed II-1 to II-2 / PDF pages 12-13: northward seasonal surface strip along California and Oregon from October to March; Vancouver Island penetration is conditional.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"monsoon-summer-sri-lanka\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"monsoon\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"Southwest Monsoon Current · June–September eastward regional reach\",\r\n      \"flow_direction\": \"eastward\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        6,\r\n        7,\r\n        8,\r\n        9\r\n      ],\r\n      \"source_season_label\": \"summer\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_file\": \"research/monsoon-summer-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_sha256\": \"1074de5de5d68f6ca753a8eafdb2fea5eaecd20204f008c6df156e3c21940f92\",\r\n      \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n      \"width_measurement_ids\": [],\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Boreal summer source convention, June–September. Historical review and section context, not a simultaneous dated trajectory or current-year climatology.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Seasonal near-surface regional geography. Historical section evidence is shallow and depth dependent; no fixed-depth velocity axis reconstructed and undercurrents excluded.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Schott and McCreary (2001), section 5.1.5, printed pp. 63–65 / PDF indices 62–64: seasonal directions/months, Sri Lanka bottleneck and separate upper-layer/undercurrent flows. August 1993 and January 1991 sections provide local latitude context, not regional axis vertices.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"monsoon-winter-sri-lanka\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"monsoon\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"Northeast Monsoon Current · November–February westward regional reach\",\r\n      \"flow_direction\": \"westward\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        11,\r\n        12,\r\n        1,\r\n        2\r\n      ],\r\n      \"source_season_label\": \"winter\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_file\": \"research/monsoon-winter-sri-lanka-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_sha256\": \"050f03273c082601dd425ad8221c6f038bcc152c4f2978e58dde9af6e60f4334\",\r\n      \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n      \"width_measurement_ids\": [],\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Boreal winter source convention, November–February. Historical review and section context, not a simultaneous dated trajectory or current-year climatology.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Seasonal near-surface regional geography. Historical section evidence is shallow and depth dependent; no fixed-depth velocity axis reconstructed and undercurrents excluded.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/schott_mccreary_41948.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Schott and McCreary (2001), section 5.1.5, printed pp. 63–65 / PDF indices 62–64: seasonal directions/months, Sri Lanka bottleneck and separate upper-layer/undercurrent flows. August 1993 and January 1991 sections provide local latitude context, not regional axis vertices.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"indian-secc-winter-reach\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"December-March eastward surface reach\",\r\n      \"flow_direction\": \"eastward\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        12,\r\n        1,\r\n        2,\r\n        3\r\n      ],\r\n      \"source_season_label\": \"winter\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_file\": \"research/indian-secc-winter-reach-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"route_candidate_sha256\": \"f4012b04e98fbddadd0d2af6636d18d04b5f89f84bbdd07cd069abdec6875ab7\",\r\n      \"geometry_role\": \"osw_editorial_reference_route\",\r\n      \"width_measurement_ids\": [],\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Source boreal winter December-March convention; Gauss-Markov seasonal climatology using 1993-2018 drifter context. Not a dated trajectory or complete annual route series.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Surface drifter climatology with GDP drogue support near 15 m and wind-slip-corrected undrogued observations; not a uniform fixed-depth current axis or full vertical extent. OSCAR upper-layer and deeper current diagnostics remain separate.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2019JC015483\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2.1-2.2: drifter support, 1993-2018 selection, fitted seasonal fields and December-March winter. Section 3 seasonal discussion after Figures 5-6: eastward SECC reaches about 90 E before recirculating into SEC; Figure 13 caption.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"comparability\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"somali\",\r\n      \"annual_length_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"reason\": \"Winter coastal branch and June-July southern limb have different source-defined spatial scopes; their nominal lengths or scenario bounds do not define annual whole-current extrema.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"davidson\",\r\n      \"annual_length_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"reason\": \"Only historical October-March California-Oregon reference geography and width context are available. April-September width and seasonal route geometry remain unknown; no modern annual cycle, seasonal extrema or uniform width footprint established.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"monsoon\",\r\n      \"annual_length_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"reason\": \"Two source-defined seasonal phases with editorial 77–83 E regional drawings. Their different latitude choices and scenario envelopes are not observed annual length minima/maxima. March–May and October geometry and all seasonal widths remain unresolved; month labels do not provide monthly velocity fields.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"annual_length_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"reason\": \"One December-March surface studied reach with editorial gates and vertices. Other seasonal axes and paired-edge widths are unavailable. Its 4400-4500 km drawing envelope is not annual length variation.\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"width_inventory_file\": \"research/ocean-current-width-inventory.json\",\r\n  \"width_inventory_sha256\": \"929527ad7c4a500eca26d495c59e6eadd3d62e82b3bc9b9cd1ff57084b1aacb8\"\r\n}\r\n","source_sha256":"5e2bbbcf1aa91253b8ca7d114765364640f62390533af513f205764af63e4422"},"routes":{"source_file":"research/ocean-current-reference-path-candidates.json","source_json":"{\r\n  \"schema\": \"osw.current-reference-path-candidates.v1\",\r\n  \"status\": \"editorial_candidates_not_canonical_length_admissions\",\r\n  \"counts\": {\r\n    \"currents_without_published_ranked_estimate\": 89,\r\n    \"currents_with_route_candidates\": 70,\r\n    \"currents_without_route_candidates\": 19,\r\n    \"route_candidates\": 76,\r\n    \"studied_reach_candidates\": 37\r\n  },\r\n  \"comparison_rule\": \"Descending length of declared OSW reference routes only. Coherent jets, specified branches and source/region-defined extents differ in scope; their order is provisional and is not a uniform whole-current ranking. Studied reaches are excluded from the reference-route order. No number replaces the existing length evidence or published ranking.\",\r\n  \"reference_route_length_order\": [\r\n    \"north-pacific-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"agulhas-return-extent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"azores-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"north-atlantic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"leeuwin-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"caribbean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"east-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"benguela-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"north-brazil-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"black-sea-rim-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"east-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"labrador-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"norwegian-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"agulhas-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"hiri-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"canary-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"somali-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"alaska-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"kuroshio-extension-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"portugal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"davidson-winter-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"tsushima-coastal-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"guinea-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"irminger-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"west-greenland-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"mindanao-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"oyashio-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"algerian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"south-australian-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"west-spitsbergen-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"zeehan-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"northern-mediterranean-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"western-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"somali-summer-southern-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"gaspe-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"balearic-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n    \"jutland-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"length_evidence_sha256\": \"c9860385231435451fdd1c989342dc73fd45ce4ac774be1a10c14576b4dfc3fc\",\r\n  \"planning_taxonomy\": {\r\n    \"status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n    \"author\": \"OSW\",\r\n    \"scope\": \"Primary construction strategy for each of the 89 inventory names without a published ranked length. Categories are work priorities, can have overlapping physical constraints, and do not establish current boundaries or comparable lengths.\",\r\n    \"input_file\": \"research/ocean-current-route-strategy-input.json\",\r\n    \"input_sha256\": \"f1b33c151b22ff56d80db60113403e6090accfb903c372048ab4cbfd9dce6036\",\r\n    \"current_ledger_sha256\": \"6c8a143208c0953512875f222154a819d5f56b7326daa6816f0609e61b4f261e\",\r\n    \"parent_taxonomy\": \"research/ocean-motion-taxonomy.json\",\r\n    \"strategies\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"split_basin_family\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Split basin families\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Shared labels need basin-specific child objects before any route length. Existing children are navigation links, not a complete family census.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Measure sourced basin members separately; create any missing child identities before route construction.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 8,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 8\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"system_route_graph\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Define system and branch graph\",\r\n        \"description\": \"A main route, component reaches and alternate branches need separate length semantics.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Specify the source-defined system, branch connectivity, depth and non-overlapping component gates; retain study reaches separately.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 3,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 2\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"continuity_hypothesis\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Keep continuity hypothesis separate\",\r\n        \"description\": \"A proposed connection cannot be ranked as an established current merely because a path can be drawn.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Audit continuity evidence and alternatives; retain hypothetical status and any proposed distance separately.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 1,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 1\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"seasonal_routes\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Construct seasonal routes\",\r\n        \"description\": \"A specified seasonal regime is needed; reversal or seasonal extensions cannot become a permanent route.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Choose sourced season, direction and layer; construct each supported seasonal path separately and preserve missing seasons.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 14,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 2\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"dated_geometry\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Construct dated or regime-specific geometry\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Variable loops, circuits and frontal paths need a specified date or regime and continuity test.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Use dated or explicitly averaged geometry, distinguish an open loop from a closed circuit, and compare repeated regimes before summarizing.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 3,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 1\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"resolve_naming_scope\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Resolve naming or extent convention\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Aliases, source-dependent limits or proposed continuity need an explicit identity/extent decision. A regional candidate may use a declared convention meanwhile.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 16,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 4\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"layer_specific_route\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Construct layer-specific paths\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Subsurface jets, undercurrents and overflows require depth, density or tracer support along the route.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Specify source layer and time support, obtain intermediate pathway geometry, and separate branches or dilution thresholds before measuring.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 13,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 1\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"expand_section_evidence\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Extend evidence beyond sections\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Cross-stream sections locate a current locally but do not define an along-stream route.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Find sourced upstream/downstream gates and continuity between sections; preserve widths and section transports as different measurements.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 5,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 0\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"preserve_survey_reach\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Preserve surveyed-reach scope\",\r\n        \"description\": \"A documented regional survey reach remains a reach until whole-flow gates are supported.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Reconstruct only the source survey reach first; obtain independent start/end evidence before proposing a broader current route.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 1,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 0\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"source_gated_regional_route\",\r\n        \"label\": \"Establish a sourced regional route\",\r\n        \"description\": \"Regional named flow or branch eligible for a declared reference convention once gates and route geography are supported. This does not assert that the flow is unbranched or steady.\",\r\n        \"next_action\": \"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.\",\r\n        \"current_count\": 25,\r\n        \"unbuilt_count\": 0\r\n      }\r\n    ]\r\n  },\r\n  \"candidates\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"indian-south-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Indian Ocean South Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_reference_path_candidate_not_scientifically_reviewed\",\r\n      \"comparison_group\": \"osw_studied_reach_routes\",\r\n      \"scope\": \"Declared 60-105 E March-May subsurface geographic reach. Approximate source longitude limits and west/east latitude context guide an OSW connecting path; not diagnosed whole-current endpoints. Surface SEC/SECC, equatorial EUC, ridge circulation loops and western/eastern extensions excluded.\",\r\n      \"route_extent_kind\": \"March-May subsurface studied reach\",\r\n      \"approximate_reference_path_km\": 5000,\r\n      \"scenario_range_km\": [\r\n        4900,\r\n        5000\r\n      ],\r\n      \"scenario_count\": 27,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2022GL098163\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Sections 2 and 3; Figure 2b caption: BRAN monthly climatology, density-layer context and approximate 60-105 E reach shifting from 8 S to 10 S. Figure 3 core threshold is a separate diagnostic.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [],\r\n      \"candidate_file\": \"research/indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"candidate_sha256\": \"09e20729d63ef0930ba1835f95fdc24285726de590f4d2c9915604358867c117\",\r\n      \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n      \"figure\": \"figures/indian-seuc-mam-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\",\r\n      \"nominal_atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"AUSW\",\r\n        \"EAFR\",\r\n        \"IND W\",\r\n        \"MONS\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_E_4\",\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Extract compatible BRAN density-layer core geometry and review ridge-scale continuity before interpreting the connecting line as an axis.\",\r\n   