 and Pizarro (2005), Data [4]–[5], surface circulation [7], STF [14]–[17] and Table 1: P18 at 103 W 33.8 S and P19 at 88 W 34.5 S. Source front/velocity distinction retained; fields and curves not digitized.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/phoc/25/1/1520-0485_1995_025_0077_tspc_2_0_co_2.xml\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Stramma, Peterson and Tomczak (1995), The South Pacific Current, JPO 25, 77–91.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Publisher-indexed abstract; direct article/PDF access unsuccessful.\",\r\n          \"supports\": \"SPC distinction from ACC, broad Chatham Rise context and possible splitting at 115–85 W. Does not assign a branch to this connection.\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2007GL030392\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Ridgway and Dunn (2007), Observational evidence for a Southern Hemisphere oceanic supergyre, GRL 34, L13612.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Section 3.4 [15]: gyre return flow and STF relation.\",\r\n          \"supports\": \"Layered gyre return flow is not universally identified by the STF; no whole-current or intermediate-layer axis copied from surface/frontal proxies.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"candidate_file\": \"research/south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"candidate_sha256\": \"8f5450e07b3d47867d57289d7bafddb502ab8b8b7f5c27d8fb67b1485f4fcedb\",\r\n      \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n      \"figure\": \"figures/south-pacific-eastern-front-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\",\r\n      \"nominal_atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"HUMB\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_A_5\",\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Diagnose a same-layer velocity axis; frontal proxy locations are not current-core locations.\",\r\n       