lier work.\",\r\n      \"supporting_sources\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://pureadmin.uhi.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/14119479/2020GL088350.pdf\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt, Claus and Hahn (2020), Fluctuations of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Associated Changes in Oxygen Transports, GRL 47, e2020GL088350, doi:10.1029/2020GL088350.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Introduction and sections 2–4, pp. 1–4: central 5 N, 23 W observations and 65–270 m definition; data intervals and fixed-box/inferred-transport distinctions.\",\r\n          \"role\": \"Central observational context; weak seasonal cycle and episodic intraseasonal events do not establish seasonal geometry.\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2018JC014760\",\r\n          \"citation\": \"Burmeister, Luebbecke, Brandt and Duteil (2019), Interannual Variability of the Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent and Its Impact on Oxygen, JGR Oceans 124, 2348–2373, doi:10.1029/2018JC014760.\",\r\n          \"locator\": \"Introduction, sections 2.1 and 2.3: 23 W ship sections; model half-width and observational integration boundaries.\",\r\n          \"role\": \"Distinguishes chosen transport integration widths and model-domain longitude span from diagnosed current dimensions.\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"candidate_file\": \"research/atlantic-neuc-reach-reference-path-candidate.json\",\r\n      \"candidate_sha256\": \"386796f3f152bc36828c6f3a1c88f262f9f8a054c1f2f3465839dae252af34ca\",\r\n      \"generator_sha256\": \"1362693ec7075e014d065691923248db455a5c3cd78c9a94880b3b472594d240\",\r\n      \"figure\": \"figures/atlantic-neuc-reach-reference-path-candidate.svg\",\r\n      \"nominal_atlas_state_crossings\": [\r\n        \"WTRA\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"recommended_nasa_tile_id\": \"level2_C_3\",\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Diagnose a compatible subsurface a