,layer,gates,fine coastline and bathymetry before physical admission.\",\r\n        \"Acquire compatible dated velocity geometry before measuring a current axis or seasonal dimensions.\",\r\n        \"Do not sum component reaches or transfer neighboring current/channel widths.\",\r\n        \"Whole-current dimensions,annual ranges,occupied width polygons,physical state containment and NASA identity remain unresolved.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"parent_current_id\": null,\r\n      \"parent_scope_note\": null,\r\n      \"ordering_sensitivity\": null\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"remaining_current_decisions\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"agulhas\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Agulhas Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"derived_lower_bound\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"The research description spans roughly 27°S–40°S; the coastal path is longer than its north–south separation. Retroflection, leakage, and the eastward Agulhas Return Current are distinct from this boundary-current core. The derived floor is unranked. A 2021 review also describes a roughly 1,000 km coastal segment. That narrower usage conflicts with the broader 27°S–40°S derived floor, so the two numbers are displayed as source-specific scopes and neither is ranked as a common whole-current length.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.vos.noaa.gov/docs/marine_info_guide.pdf\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"agulhas-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"western boundary current\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"source_gated_regional_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Establish a sourced regional route\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"The research description spans roughly 27°S–40°S; the coastal path is longer than its north–south separation. Retroflection, leakage, and the eastward Agulhas Return Current are distinct from this boundary-current core. The derived floor is unranked. A 2021 review also describes a roughly 1,000 km coastal segment. That narrower usage conflicts with the broader 27°S–40°S derived floor, so the two numbers are displayed as source-specific scopes and neither is ranked as a common whole-current length.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"agulhas-return\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Agulhas Return Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"derived_lower_bound\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"The hydrographic survey distinguishes the Agulhas Return Current from the Agulhas Current and traces its weakening eastward flow toward the Crozet Basin. This derived distance floor is not a measured streamline, whole-current length, or the length of the westward Agulhas Current.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.cfoo.co.za/seaatlas/papers/agulhas_return_current.pdf\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"agulhas-return-extent-reference-path-candidate\",\r\n        \"agulhas-return-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"eastward frontal return current\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"source_gated_regional_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Establish a sourced regional route\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"The hydrographic survey distinguishes the Agulhas Return Current from the Agulhas Current and traces its weakening eastward flow toward the Crozet Basin. This derived distance floor is not a measured streamline, whole-current length, or the length of the westward Agulhas Current.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"alaska\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Alaska Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"alaska-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"subpolar boundary current\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"source_gated_regional_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Establish a sourced regional route\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"No comparable path-length estimate admitted yet.\",\r\n      \"next_action\"