unranked.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2006GL026965\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"deep-western-boundary-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"deep western boundary current\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"system_route_graph\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Define system and branch graph\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"The study identifies southward deep western boundary flow at 47°, 36°, and 24.5°N in decadal inverse solutions. This is a North Atlantic segment only; sections from different cruises do not establish one simultaneous continuous path or a whole-Atlantic current length. The derived floor is unranked.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Specify the source-defined system, branch connectivity, depth and non-overlapping component gates; retain study reaches separately.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"east-adriatic\",\r\n      \"name\": \"East Adriatic Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"2002–2003 measurements off the eastern Adriatic coast establish a variable current that strengthened in January–February and again in May. Its Dalmatian coastal reach may overlap the older Dalmatian Current name, but that synonymy is not yet established; no full path length is admitted.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1029/2005JC003271\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"east-adriatic-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"northwestward coastal boundary current\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"resolve_naming_scope\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Resolve naming or extent convention\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"2002–2003 measurements off the eastern Adriatic coast establish a variable current that strengthened in January–February and again in May. Its Dalmatian coastal reach may overlap the older Dalmatian Current name, but that synonymy is not yet established; no full path length is admitted.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Read competing definitions, resolve aliases versus distinct flows, and retain source-convention routes without merging their extents.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"east-australian\",\r\n      \"name\": \"East Australian Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"derived_lower_bound\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"A derived minimum north–south span for the coherent shelf-break jet only; not a measured streamline or a published whole-current length. Separation and extension shift over time.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.vos.noaa.gov/docs/marine_info_guide.pdf\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"east-australian-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"western boundary current\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"source_gated_regional_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Establish a sourced regional route\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"A derived minimum north–south span for the coherent shelf-break jet only; not a measured streamline or a published whole-current length. Separation and extension shift over time.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"east-greenland-coastal\",\r\n      \"name\": \"East Greenland Coastal Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"sampled_reach_only\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"A summer 2004 hydrographic and velocity survey identified this inner-shelf branch along the approximately 1,000 km southeast Greenland shelf south of Denmark Strait. That is a documented regional reach, not a measured whole-current path or a year-round length; the offshore East Greenland Current is distinct.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"east-greenland-coastal-reach-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"low-salinity inner-shelf coastal jet\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"preserve_survey_reach\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Preserve surveyed-reach scope\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"A summer 2004 hydrographic and velocity survey identified this inner-shelf branch along the approximately 1,000 km southeast Greenland shelf south of Denmark Strait. That is a documented regional reach, not a measured whole-current path or a year-round length; the offshore East Greenland Current is distinct.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Reconstruct only the source survey reach first; obtain independent start/end evidence before proposing a broader current route.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"east-greenland\",\r\n      \"name\": \"East Greenland Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"derived_lower_bound\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"The study distinguishes the outer East Greenland Current from the coastal branch and assesses the system between the 78.5°N Fram Strait section and Cape Farewell. The coast-following route may be longer than the north–south separation; no comparable whole-current centerline length is admitted, so this regional floor is unranked.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"east-greenland-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"polar boundary current\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"source_gated_regional_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Establish a sourced regional route\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"The study distinguishes the outer East Greenland Current from the coastal branch and assesses the system between the 78.5°N Fram Strait section and Cape Farewell. The coast-following route may be longer than the north–south separation; no comparable whole-current centerline length is admitted, so this regional floor is unranked.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Review the existing editorial route against scientific gates; broader/system/family scope remains governed by the planning strategy.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Read primary geographic definitions, choose explicit endpoint/branch/layer/time conventions, and measure a reviewed route with alternatives; naming points alone are insufficient.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"not_assessed_by_this_planning_crosswalk\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"Umbrella label for multiple eastward tropical countercurrents. North and South named families and basin-specific flows require separate boundaries and length estimates.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"reference_path_not_constructed\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"equatorial current family\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"split_basin_family\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Split basin families\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"Umbrella label for multiple eastward tropical countercurrents. North and South named families and basin-specific flows require separate boundaries and length estimates.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Measure sourced basin members separately; create any missing child identities before route construction.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Measure sourced basin members separately; create any missing child identities before route construction.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"North Equatorial Countercurrent\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"south-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"South Equatorial Countercurrent\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"known_component_records_not_complete_census\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"A shared subsurface name across three basins. The Indian Ocean expression is weaker and seasonal; component currents require separate boundaries and length estimates.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/glossary.html\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"reference_path_not_constructed\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"subsurface equatorial current family\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"split_basin_family\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Split basin families\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_planning_crosswalk_not_scientific_classification_approval\",\r\n      \"planning_basis\": \"A shared subsurface name across three basins. The Indian Ocean expression is weaker and seasonal; component currents require separate boundaries and length estimates.\",\r\n      \"next_action\": \"Measure sourced basin members separately; create any missing child identities before route construction.\",\r\n      \"strategy_next_action\": \"Measure sourced basin members separately; create any missing child identities before route construction.\",\r\n      \"known_component_currents\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"pacific-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Pacific Equatorial Undercurrent\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"atlantic-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Atlantic Equatorial Undercurrent\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"current_id\": \"indian-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n          \"name\": \"Indian Ocean Equatorial Undercurrent\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"component_inventory_status\": \"known_component_records_not_complete_census\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"current_id\": \"gaspe\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Gaspé Current\",\r\n      \"existing_length_evidence_status\": \"no_numeric_length\",\r\n      \"existing_scope\": \"The source places the jet along the Gaspé Peninsula and reports a typical width of about 10–20 km near its strongest reach; width is not along-current length, and no comparable whole-current estimate is admitted.\",\r\n      \"name_source_url\": \"https://www.marineregions.org/gazetteer.php?p=details&id=30052\",\r\n      \"candidate_ids\": [\r\n        \"gaspe-reference-path-candidate\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"reference_path_decision\": \"editorial_candidate_present_scientific_review_pending\",\r\n      \"published_length_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"ledger_kind\": \"buoyancy-driven coastal jet\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_id\": \"source_gated_regional_route\",\r\n      \"route_strategy_label\": \"Establish a sourced regional route\",\r\n      \"planning_status\": \"editorial_