029/2003JC002146. Institutional author versions.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Part2 author version printed p6/PDF7, R13 velocity-width description; part1 printed p5/PDF6 and Fig9 printed p22/PDF23, reference method; Table1 printed p13/PDF14, occupation context.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-14\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"author_reported_companion_study_geostrophic_spatial_scale\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Transcribed explicit width descriptions from original part2; checked companion part1 method, Fig9 and occupation table. No curve digitization.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"R13 faster geostrophic peak description\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"regional_summary\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"uncertainty_km\": null,\r\n      \"whole_current_width_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Source warns about geostrophic accuracy and reference choice. No contemporaneous R13/R12 ADCP; missing D2 data. Width edge cutoff and numerical width error unspecified.\",\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Recover original paired velocity edges and exact width-occupation linkage.\",\r\n        \"Review reference sensitivity and flow identification before physical width inference.\",\r\n        \"Independent scientific admission.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"original_regional_context\": {\r\n        \"description_kind\": \"gogp99_geostrophic_spatial_scale\",\r\n        \"spatial_operator\": \"peak\",\r\n        \"typical_or_peak_velocity_m_s\": 0.4,\r\n        \"velocity_boundary_threshold_m_s\": null,\r\n        \"velocity_description_is_boundary_cutoff\": false,\r\n        \"velocity_reference_depth_m\": 30,\r\n        \"added_reference_velocity_m_s\": 0.09,\r\n        \"reference_velocity_is_contemporaneous_adcp\": false,\r\n        \"r13_r12_adcp_available\": false,\r\n        \"d2_returned_data\": false,\r\n        \"transport_partition_depth_m\": 45,\r\n        \"reference_or_transport_depth_is_width_layer\": false,\r\n        \"method_figure_section\": \"R13b\",\r\n        \"width_description_section\": \"R13\",\r\n        \"width_occupation_date_verified\": false,\r\n        \"r13_occupation_dates_context\": [\r\n          \"1999-10-11\",\r\n          \"1999-10-22\",\r\n          \"1999-11-02\"\r\n        ],\r\n        \"earlier_reference_year_is_width_year\": false,\r\n        \"salinity_width_is_velocity_width\": false,\r\n        \"band_and_peak_are_independent_occupations\": false,\r\n        \"band_peak_difference_is_error_or_seasonal_range\": false,\r\n        \"boundary_coordinates_extracted\": false,\r\n        \"display_aria_label\": \"Persian Gulf outflow: approximately 5 km faster geostrophic peak. Reference-dependent geostrophic description, not an ADCP width or specified edge threshold. The 30 km band and 5 km peak are distinct operators, not annual extrema or uncertainty.\",\r\n        \"display_caption\": \"About 5 km: faster geostrophic peak near 0.4 m/s. A spatial description at R13; the stated speed is not an extracted width cutoff.\",\r\n        \"display_method_note\": \"GOGP99 1999 context; 30 m reference plus 0.09 m/s mean offset. No R13/R12 ADCP returned. Exact width occupation, fixed layer, geographic edges and width error unknown. The band/peak and salinity-core widths are separate definitions.\",\r\n        \"comparison_figure\": \"figures/persian-gulf-gogp99-geostrophic-scales.svg\",\r\n        \"comparison_figure_label\": \"Compare the flow band and faster peak\",\r\n        \"audit_file\": \"research/persian-gulf-gogp99-geostrophic-scales-scope-audit.json\",\r\n        \"audit_sha256\": \"6f4a7c211cb02fc5906c5d6e98279022bec688f446a1ba20aa7aa79a6c2d28d1\",\r\n        \"audit_pointer\": \"/measurements/1\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"atlantic-seuc-molinari-1981-core-width\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"atlantic-south-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Atlantic South Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_regional_summary\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_velocity_contour_core_span\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 120,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"One approximate author-reported 20 cm/s core width. Abstract approximately 100 km is separate unreconciled context, not an endpoint, error or independent occupation.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Eastern and western Atlantic sections: approximately 25–29 W and 4 W, within the 1978–1980 study. Not the newer 35 W ledger section or the entire current.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Source cross-current sections; no geographic edge pair or exact flow-normal projection extracted.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Subthermocline 20 cm/s isotach core. Reported core depths and vertical extent are context, not fixed width-layer limits.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Author summary across six 1978–1980 cruises. Individual figure dates do not date this characteristic width; no per-cruise or seasonal width series extracted.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Source defines the core as flow within the 20 cm/s isotach and reports about 120 km core width. This is not the net-flow boundary.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://archimer.ifremer.fr/doc/00121/23229/21063.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Molinari, R. L., Voituriez, B., and Duncan, P. (1981), Observations in the subthermocline undercurrent of the Equatorial South Atlantic Ocean: 1978–1980, Oceanologica Acta 4(4), 451–456.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Printed p453/PDF p3, core definition and width paragraphs; abstract p451/PDF p1; methods/captions p452/PDF p2; net-flow boundary limitation p456/PDF p6.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-14\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_original_campaign_core_summary\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Transcribed the explicit contour-defined body core width after original-page review; no figure digitization or geographic edge inference.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"1978–1980 study · 20 cm/s core summary\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"regional_summary\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"uncertainty_km\": null,\r\n      \"whole_current_width_km\": null,\r\n      \"annual_width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Body about 120 km versus abstract about 100 km retained separately. Reference captions use 1000 db while prose uses 1000 m. Numerical width uncertainty and net-flow boundaries unknown.\",\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Resolve source approximate-width description discrepancy without manufacturing a range.\",\r\n        \"Recover paired geographic edges and compatible repeated sections before mapping or annual variability.\",\r\n        \"Independent scientific admission.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"original_regional_context\": {\r\n        \"description_kind\": \"atlantic_seuc_contour_core_summary\",\r\n        \"core_threshold_cm_s\": 20,\r\n        \"abstract_description_width_km\": 100,\r\n        \"body_core_width_km\": 120,\r\n        \"abstract_body_discrepancy_reconciled\": false,\r\n        \"descriptions_are_independent_occupations\": false,\r\n        \"descriptions_define_range_or_error\": false,\r\n        \"geostrophic_reference_prose\": \"1000 m\",\r\n        \"geostrophic_reference_figure_captions\": \"1000 db\",\r\n        \"pressure_depth_expressions_are_exact_conversion\": false,\r\n        \"pcm_velocity_reference_depths_m\": [\r\n          500,\r\n          600\r\n        ],\r\n        \"velocity_references_are_width_layer\": false,\r\n        \"abstract_core_depth_context_m\": [\r\n          150,\r\n          200\r\n        ],\r\n        \"core_depth_context_is_fixed_width_layer\": false,\r\n        \"velocity_errors_are_width_uncertainty\": false,\r\n        \"float_sampling_band_is_width\": false,\r\n        \"newer_35w_section_is_measurement_support\": false,\r\n        \"net_flow_boundaries_resolved\": false,\r\n        \"per_cruise_width_values_available\": false,\r\n        \"campaign_years\": [\r\n          1978,\r\n          1979,\r\n          1980\r\n        ],\r\n        \"display_aria_label\": \"Atlantic SEUC: about 120 km 20 cm/s core width in the 1978–1980 study. Abstract about 100 km remains separate unresolved context, not a range or uncertainty. No fixed depth or annual width inferred.\",\r\n        \"display_caption\": \"About 120 km · source-defined 20 cm/s core. The abstract separately says about 100 km; no combined 100–120 km range or 110 km midpoint.\",\r\n        \"display_method_note\": \"1978–1980 regional summary; no width per cruise, fixed depth, numerical width error or net-flow boundary. 1000 db captions and 1000 m prose retained as distinct reference expressions.\",\r\n        \"comparison_figure\": \"figures/atlantic-seuc-molinari-1981-core-width.svg\",\r\n        \"audit_file\": \"research/atlantic-seuc-molinari-1981-core-width-scope-audit.json\",\r\n        \"audit_sha256\": \"577cccac98a3970272e7e2ab7a11bceba86138fec881adad570ba18d58c8ca1c\"\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"northern-mediterranean-winter-width\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"northern-mediterranean\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Northern Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_regional_seasonal_summary\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_current_width\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 25,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"No numerical uncertainty interval supplied for this approximate seasonal value.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Southern French coast / Gulf of Lion regional literature context; not a uniform width along the full Ligurian-Catalan route.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Not fixed in this regional synthesis.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Current envelope described with approximate seasonal vertical extent 450 m; width is not a measurement at every depth or a fixed-depth slice.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"winter seasonal description in source introduction; not the December 2011 survey measurement.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author-reported width; a reproducible speed threshold or paired boundary coordinates is not supplied in this introductory summary.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/14/689/2018/\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Berta et al. (2018), Wind-induced variability in the Northern Current (northwestern Mediterranean Sea) as depicted by a multi-platform observing system, Ocean Science 14, 689-710, doi:10.5194/os-14-689-2018.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 1, paragraph beginning It exhibits a marked annual cycle; preceding paragraph gives regional observation context.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_synthesis_of_prior_observations\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Approximate numerical width transcribed from prose; no figure or route buffer 