01007\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Bower, Serra and Ambar (2002), Structure of the Mediterranean Undercurrent and Mediterranean Water spreading around the southwestern Iberian Peninsula, doi:10.1029/2001JC001007.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 2 [9]; Section 3.1 [16]-[18], Figure 5 caption and section 3.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_observational_analysis\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Approximate prose value transcribed with its detailed boundary definition; no figure digitized.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Review boundary definition and regional/layer sampling.\",\r\n        \"Obtain comparable repeated observations before seasonal animation or annual range.\",\r\n        \"Canonical measurement admission and release review.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"May 1993: Portimao section\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"survey_summary\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"width_metric_label\": \"synoptic geostrophic flow-band width\",\r\n      \"boundary_sides\": \"source_reported_band\",\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"A synoptic geostrophic band and an ensemble core-to-offshore-edge span use different methods and boundaries.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"davidson-historical-winter-width\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"davidson\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Davidson Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_regional_seasonal_summary\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_current_width\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 64,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"One approximate historical regional value; no numerical uncertainty, repeated seasonal widths or annual extrema supplied.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"California and Oregon coastal strip described by the 1978 report. Possible penetration into Vancouver Island waters is conditional and does not extend this width assignment.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Not specified in this regional synthesis; no flow-normal section reconstructed.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Seasonal surface current; distinct from the separately described California Undercurrent below 200 m.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"October-March regional seasonal description in a February 1978 report; strongest flow described in January. Not a dated width survey, current-year observation or modern monthly climatology.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author-reported approximate width; paired boundary coordinates, velocity threshold and sampling method are not specified.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://waves-vagues.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/library-bibliotheque/40591190_v2.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Fisheries and Environment Canada, Working Group on West Coast Deepwater Oil Ports (1978), Potential Pacific Coast Oil Ports: A Comparative Environmental Risk Analysis, Volume II - Supplementary Appendices, February 1978.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Appendix II, section II.1, printed II-1 to II-2 (PDF pages 12-13), paragraph beginning The Davidson current; width and months on PDF page 13.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_publication_year\": 1978,\r\n      \"source_document_sha256\": \"ea4f05cbba6f7b955ba26a93359e237dc041f6d3c2dcbb4cc6ea11ce455dd6c6\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_historical_regional_synthesis\",\r\n      \"historical_summary\": true,\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Approximate 64 km and October-March interval transcribed from full PDF prose. No figure digitized, route buffered or station distance interpreted as width.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Review underlying observations, width boundaries and historical applicability.\",\r\n        \"Obtain regional repeated seasonal observations before annual variability or modern representative width.\",\r\n        \"Canonical measurement admission and release review.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"October-March (1978 regional summary)\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"seasonal_summary\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": [\r\n        10,\r\n        11,\r\n        12,\r\n        1,\r\n        2,\r\n        3\r\n      ],\r\n      \"calendar_source_locator\": \"Appendix II section II.1, printed II-2 / PDF page 13: October to March along California and Oregon coasts.\",\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Historical regional summary from 1978, not a present-day width measurement. Vancouver Island penetration is conditional; 25 and 50 km off Tofino are observation locations, not width boundaries. The separately described 50 km California Undercurrent is a different layer and current.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"gaspe-regional-typical-width-range\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"gaspe\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Gaspé Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_regional_summary\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_current_width\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": null,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": [\r\n        10,\r\n        20\r\n      ],\r\n      \"range_kind\": \"reported_typical_regional_width_span\",\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Source-reported typical regional width span; no single midpoint or representative width selected. Not a confidence interval, matched seasonal pair or annual extrema.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Gaspe Peninsula coastal jet described in thesis introductory regional synthesis; not a measured uniform width along the estuary-to-Magdalen reference corridor.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Not specified for this typical regional prose range.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Upper coastal jet, described in the first approximately 40 m; range not assigned to every depth.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Regional typical-width summary in February 2022 thesis introduction; the adjacent summer maximum-speed clause does not make this a measured summer width range. No matched winter/summer widths or dated survey interval assigned.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author-reported typical width; no paired boundary coordinates or reproducible velocity threshold supplied for the range.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://semaphore.uqar.ca/2055/1/Theau_Leclercq_fevrier2022.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Leclercq, Théau (2022), Observations des remontées et des plongées des eaux en bordure du courant de Gaspé, master's thesis in oceanography, UQAR-ISMER, February 2022.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Printed page 5 / PDF page 21, paragraph on typical width 10-20 km; printed page 14 / PDF page 30, English introduction, width can reach 20 km.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_publication_year\": 2022,\r\n      \"source_document_sha256\": \"b8244831f7e593b0f5da2861f44658ccc8e9c4822cb9fe3b122e2e1e5654ae25\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_regional_literature_summary\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Typical 10-20 km range transcribed from full thesis prose, with corroborating English upper-width statement. No figure digitized, midpoint manufactured or route buffered.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Review original observational definitions and temporal/along-route support behind the synthesis.\",\r\n        \"Obtain paired boundaries and compatible repeat sections before seasonal widths, annual ranges or representative width.\",\r\n        \"Canonical measurement admission and release review.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"Regional typical width (2022 synthesis)\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"regional_summary\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Literature summary in an observational thesis, not a new dated width measurement from its transects. Exact boundaries and uncertainty remain unspecified.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"north-cape-northern-2007-profile-scale\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"north-cape\",\r\n      \"name\": \"North Cape Current — Northern branch\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_survey_profile_fit_scale\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"gaussian_e_folding_distance_from_profile_center\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 8,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Approximate fitted effective scale; no fit confidence interval or annual variability range supplied.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Northern branch near the western Hopen Deep / Spitsbergen Bank polar frontal zone, Barents Sea. Not the Central branch or whole North Cape system.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Distance from frontal-section center across individual crossings; northward geographic velocity component fitted. Exact paired geographic boundaries unresolved.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Composite vertical support unresolved. Fig. 9 specifies a 20–80 m average for LS05; Fig. 10 does not explicitly establish that same fixed layer for all 15 crossings. Instrument generally sampled from about 20 m to 150 m or 15 m above bottom.\",\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"15 frontal crossings during summer expeditions in 2007. Paper describes a 29 May–10 June 2007 cruise, but exact composite sampling bounds are unresolved; not a recurring seasonal width.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Source approximates the mean northward velocity profile by V(x)=17 exp(-(x/8)^2), x in km and V in cm/s, and calls 8 km mean effective width. OSW infers center-to-e-folding scale from the equation; no paired-edge full span is admitted.\",\r\n      \"boundary_sides\": \"fitted_center_to_e_folding_distance\",\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://physical-oceanography.ru/repository/issues/2017/02/05/20170205.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Morozov, Pavlov, Pavlova and Fedorov (2017), Polar Frontal Zone of the Barents Sea Western Trough Based on the Direct Measurements in 2007, Physical Oceanography 2, 36–50, doi:10.22449/1573-160X-2017-2-36-50.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Abstract; Introduction pp. 36–37; Instruments p. 37; Stationary currents p. 38; Currents pp. 45–47, Fig. 9 and Fig. 10, especially Gaussian-fit paragraph on p. 47.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_front_centered_velocity_profile_fit\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Transcribed source fit scale and 15-crossing count; metric interpretation inferred algebraically from stated Gaussian equation. No figure digitized or converted full width added.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"survey_profile_composite\",\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"2007 frontal-crossing composite\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"cruise_context_period\": {\r\n        \"start\": \"2007-05-29\",\r\n        \"end\": \"2007-06-10\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"cruise_context_is_composite_sampling_bounds\": false,\r\n      \"profile_fit\": {\r\n        \"model\": \"gaussian\",\r\n        \"equation\": \"V(x)=A*exp(-(x/a)^2)\",\r\n        \"amplitude\": 17,\r\n        \"velocity_units\": \"cm/s\",\r\n        \"scale_km\": 8,\r\n        \"coordinate_units\": \"km\",\r\n        \"component\": \"northward_geographic_velocity\",\r\n        \"center_definition\": \"frontal_section_center\",\r\n        \"crossing_count\": 15,\r\n        \"parameter_interpretation\": \"center_to_e_folding_distance\",\r\n        \"interpretation_origin\": \"OSW_algebraic_inference_from_source_equation\",\r\n        \"fit_uncertainty_km\": null\r\n      },\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Resolve exact composite depth averaging and crossing dates from underlying data.\",\r\n        \"Define comparable paired boundaries before any full-width comparison.\",\r\n        \"Review branch identity and along-route support; canonical admission remains pending.\"\r\n      ]\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"atlantic-neuc-1993-02-angular-section-span\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"atlantic-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_month_section_angular_span\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_meridional_angular_span\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 220,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Published approximate two-degree latitude span, converted to kilometres; no source uncertainty range and no annual/seasonal variability interval.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"35 W section near 5 N; reported latitude width for this historical survey. Not a uniform along-route width.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Reported meridional section span; no exact flow-normal reinterpretation or observed paired-edge geometry.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Historical subsurface NEUC velocity-core context near sigma-theta 26.75 kg/m3; full width at every depth and fixed-depth bounds unresolved.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"February 1993 source section; month precision only, exact occupation days unresolved. Not a seasonal climatology.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author reports a two-degree latitude width centered at 5 N. Lateral velocity threshold unspecified; no threshold or observed edge coordinates inferred.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Bourles, Gouriou and Chuchla (1999), On the circulation in the upper layer of the western equatorial Atlantic, JGR Oceans 104(C9), 21151–21170, doi:10.1029/1999JC900058.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 4.8, p. 21163: 35 W sections in February 1993 and April 1996, centered at 5 N with two-degree latitude width; Figs. 3c and 3e.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_month_hydrographic_velocity_section\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Source angular width transcribed; WGS84 meridional unit conversion centered at reported latitude, rounded to 10 km. Normalization limits are computation only, not observed edges; no source figure digitized.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Independent scientific extraction review and canonical admission.\",\r\n        \"Diagnose lateral boundaries and compatible repeated sections before full-width or seasonal dimensions.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"February 1993 section\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"month_dated_section\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"width_metric_label\": \"author-reported meridional section span\",\r\n      \"observed_month\": \"1993-02\",\r\n      \"time_precision\": \"month\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"boundary_sides\": \"author_reported_section_span\",\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"angular_span_conversion\": {\r\n        \"source_reported_latitude_span_degrees\": 2,\r\n        \"source_reported_center_latitude_degrees\": 5,\r\n        \"source_section_longitude_degrees_east\": -35,\r\n        \"method\": \"WGS84_meridional_distance_centered_for_unit_conversion_only\",\r\n        \"normalization_limits_are_observed_edges\": false,\r\n        \"unrounded_distance_km\": 221.16564339691212,\r\n        \"rounding_km\": 10\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"atlantic-neuc-1996-04-angular-section-span\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"atlantic-north-equatorial-undercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Atlantic North Equatorial Undercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_month_section_angular_span\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_meridional_angular_span\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 220,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Published approximate two-degree latitude span, converted to kilometres; no source uncertainty range and no annual/seasonal variability interval.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"35 W section near 5 N; reported latitude width for this historical survey. Not a uniform along-route width.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Reported meridional section span; no exact flow-normal reinterpretation or observed paired-edge geometry.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Historical subsurface NEUC velocity-core context near sigma-theta 26.75 kg/m3; full width at every depth and fixed-depth bounds unresolved.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"April 1996 source section; month precision only, exact occupation days unresolved. Not a seasonal climatology.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author reports a two-degree latitude width centered at 5 N. Lateral velocity threshold unspecified; no threshold or observed edge coordinates inferred.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://horizon.documentation.ird.fr/exl-doc/pleins_textes/pleins_textes_7/b_fdi_51-52/010019670.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Bourles, Gouriou and Chuchla (1999), On the circulation in the upper layer of the western equatorial Atlantic, JGR Oceans 104(C9), 21151–21170, doi:10.1029/1999JC900058.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 4.8, p. 21163: 35 W sections in February 1993 and April 1996, centered at 5 N with two-degree latitude width; Figs. 3c and 3e.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_month_hydrographic_velocity_section\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Source angular width transcribed; WGS84 meridional unit conversion centered at reported latitude, rounded to 10 km. Normalization limits are computation only, not observed edges; no source figure digitized.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Independent scientific extraction review and canonical admission.\",\r\n        \"Diagnose lateral boundaries and compatible repeated sections before full-width or seasonal dimensions.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"April 1996 section\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"month_dated_section\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"width_metric_label\": \"author-reported meridional section span\",\r\n      \"observed_month\": \"1996-04\",\r\n      \"time_precision\": \"month\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"boundary_sides\": \"author_reported_section_span\",\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"angular_span_conversion\": {\r\n        \"source_reported_latitude_span_degrees\": 2,\r\n        \"source_reported_center_latitude_degrees\": 5,\r\n        \"source_section_longitude_degrees_east\": -35,\r\n        \"method\": \"WGS84_meridional_distance_centered_for_unit_conversion_only\",\r\n        \"normalization_limits_are_observed_edges\": false,\r\n        \"unrounded_distance_km\": 221.16564339691212,\r\n        \"rounding_km\": 10\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"ligurian-menton-nice-composite-profile-band\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"ligurian\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Ligurian Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_composite_coast_distance_flow_band\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"author_reported_offshore_flow_band_span\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 20,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Difference between source-reported 15 and 35 km coast-distance limits; those are positions, not a 15–35 km width range, statistical uncertainty or seasonal margin.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Local Menton–Nice Northern Current profile, assigned to the Ligurian regional segment under the OSW ledger convention. Not representative of the whole segment or broader Northern Current.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Source cross-shore coast-distance coordinate in local along-shore velocity profiles; exact flow-normal section geometry unresolved.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Surface-flow geography in a study combining CODE drifters following the first metre and ARGOSPHERE drifters following the first 10–20 cm with unquantified wind slip. No full-depth or shelf-break axis diagnosed from the editorial route.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"Intermittent coastal drifter profile composite: June–October 2007 and October–November 2008 source context. No exact local-band sampling dates, continuous observation period or seasonal climatology.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Author describes the main offshore flow band between 15 and 35 km from coast off Menton–Nice. Span is about 20 km; boundary velocity threshold unspecified. Inshore highly variable flow is not silently included.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://mrea.sincem.unibo.it/images/reports/2011_Poulain_Aspects_of_the_surface_circulation.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Poulain, Gerin, Rixen, Zanasca, Teixeira, Griffa, Molcard, de Marte and Pinardi (2012), Aspects of the surface circulation in the Liguro-Provencal basin and Gulf of Lion as observed by satellite-tracked drifters (2007–2009), Bollettino di Geofisica Teorica ed Applicata 53(2), 261–279, doi:10.4430/bgta0052.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 4, pp. 273–274, Fig. 9b and Discussion p. 276: local flow between 15 and 35 km from coast; section 2.1 distinguishes surface drifter types.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_composite_surface_velocity_profile\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Source-reported offshore band positions transcribed; subtract 35 minus 15 km for approximately 20 km local band span. No curve digitized, velocity threshold fitted or map footprint constructed.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Independent source-extraction and segment-assignment review.\",\r\n        \"Resolve local physical boundaries and wind slip before an occupied footprint or depth-wide width.\",\r\n        \"Obtain compatible repeated seasonal observations before annual dimension ranges.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"Menton–Nice surface profile composite\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"ensemble_profile_band\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"width_metric_label\": \"reported offshore flow-band span\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"boundary_sides\": \"reported_coast_distance_band_limits\",\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"sampling_windows_are_exact_observation_bounds\": false,\r\n      \"sampling_context_month_windows\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"start\": \"2007-06\",\r\n          \"end\": \"2007-10\"\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n          \"start\": \"2008-10\",\r\n          \"end\": \"2008-11\"\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"coast_distance_profile\": {\r\n        \"source_reported_band_limits_km\": [\r\n          15,\r\n          35\r\n        ],\r\n        \"span_calculation\": \"farther_minus_nearer_coast_distance\",\r\n        \"boundary_velocity_threshold_m_s\": null,\r\n        \"cross_shore_bin_km\": 4,\r\n        \"along_shore_bin_km\": 30,\r\n        \"cross_shore_overlap_percent\": 50\r\n      },\r\n      \"source_current_label\": \"Northern Current\",\r\n      \"source_parent_current_id\": \"northern-mediterranean\",\r\n      \"segment_assignment_role\": \"OSW_editorial_parent_flow_regional_segment_assignment\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"east-greenland-coastal-2004-cape-farewell-threshold-section\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"east-greenland-coastal\",\r\n      \"name\": \"East Greenland Coastal Current\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_relative_velocity_section_span\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"relative_inner_jet_velocity_threshold_span\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 30,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"No numeric source width uncertainty or annual range extracted.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"Cape Farewell JR105 section 1 near 60 N; not the entire southeast Greenland shelf.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Cross-shelf survey section; exact endpoints not digitized.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Gridded absolute geostrophic velocity referenced to shipboard ADCP; no fixed depth averaging layer extracted. The separate 75 m frontal depth scale is not width-layer thickness.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"July-August 2004 JR105 campaign; exact occupation date of section 1 not extracted. Not a recurring summer phase or climatology.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Lateral bounds where velocity decreases to 15% of the maximum inner jet velocity; width scale wobs. The separately defined depth scale uses the 34-isohaline at the bottom.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.whoi.edu/cms/files/Sutherland_EGCC_revised_withfigs_33743.pdf\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Sutherland and Pickart (2008), The East Greenland Coastal Current: Structure, variability, and forcing. Accepted manuscript, Progress in Oceanography.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 2.1: July-August 2004 JR105; Section 2.3: absolute geostrophic velocity reference; Section 3.1, PDF pages 9-10: 15% lateral criterion and Cape Farewell wobs = 30 km.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_observational_analysis\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Author-reported prose width and threshold transcribed; no section figure or velocity field digitized.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Review boundary definition and regional/layer sampling.\",\r\n        \"Obtain comparable repeated observations before seasonal animation or annual range.\",\r\n        \"Canonical measurement admission and release review.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"2004 Cape Farewell section\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"survey_threshold_section\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"width_metric_label\": \"local section width at 15% of maximum inner jet velocity\",\r\n      \"boundary_sides\": \"paired_relative_velocity_boundaries\",\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"Source uses 3-5 km station spacing and 3 km by 10 m gridding. Reported 75 m frontal depth scale is separate; no fine boundary accuracy inferred.\",\r\n      \"velocity_threshold_fraction\": 0.15,\r\n      \"velocity_reference_statistic\": \"maximum_inner_jet_velocity\",\r\n      \"campaign_month_window\": {\r\n        \"start_month\": \"2004-07\",\r\n        \"end_month\": \"2004-08\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"sampling_window_is_exact_section_dates\": false,\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"atlantic-necc-hs5-mean-zero-contour-width\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"atlantic-north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Atlantic North Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_mean_section_width\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"mean_cross_section_zero_crossing_span\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 860,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Published approximate mean-field section width; no error interval. Two sections do not supply seasonal or annual extrema.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"HS5 at 42 W; source NECC mean section band, not one branch or a whole-current width.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Source cross-section component; not a reconstructed flow-normal section.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Altimetry-derived surface geostrophic field; no fixed-depth bounds inferred.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"January 1993-December 2017 mean velocity-profile context; month precision. Not a mean of daily widths or a dated section.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Paired zero contours of the mean signed cross-section velocity; eastward positive. Half-peak intensity domain is a different definition.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.org/articles/19/251/2023/os-19-251-2023.html\",\r\n      \"source_citation\": \"Dimoune et al. (2023), Ocean Science 19, 251-268, doi:10.5194/os-19-251-2023.\",\r\n      \"source_locator\": \"Section 3 width paragraphs after Fig. 3 discussion: NECC5/NECC6 widths and zero-contour definition; section 2.1 data/method. HTML table caption is Table 1 while prose references Table 2.\",\r\n      \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-03\",\r\n      \"source_evidence_kind\": \"published_mean_geostrophic_section_profile\",\r\n      \"extraction_method\": \"Transcribed author-reported numerical section widths and definition; no figure or velocity array digitized.\",\r\n      \"whole_current_representative\": false,\r\n      \"width_rank_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"remaining_gates\": [\r\n        \"Independent extraction and method review; no canonical admission.\",\r\n        \"Obtain matched branch/month edge geometry before seasonal widths.\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"phase_label\": \"HS5 mean section (42 W)\",\r\n      \"phase_kind\": \"mean_velocity_section\",\r\n      \"observed_period\": null,\r\n      \"width_metric_label\": \"mean-field zero-contour section span\",\r\n      \"calendar_months\": null,\r\n      \"fixed_layer_bounds_m\": null,\r\n      \"boundary_sides\": \"paired_mean_zero_contours\",\r\n      \"full_width_inference_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"annual_extrema_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"seasonal_playback_eligible\": false,\r\n      \"is_confidence_interval\": false,\r\n      \"mean_section_context\": {\r\n        \"section_longitude_degrees_east\": -42,\r\n        \"averaging_period_months\": {\r\n          \"start\": \"1993-01\",\r\n          \"end\": \"2017-12\"\r\n        },\r\n        \"velocity_boundary_m_s\": 0,\r\n        \"averaging_before_boundary_detection\": true,\r\n        \"is_mean_of_instantaneous_widths\": false\r\n      },\r\n      \"source_quality_note\": \"0.25-degree optimally interpolated product and geostrophic assumptions limit boundary precision; ageostrophic contributions omitted. Mean band is not the width of the editorial summer route.\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"atlantic-necc-hs6-mean-zero-contour-width\",\r\n      \"current_id\": \"atlantic-north-equatorial-countercurrent\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Atlantic North Equatorial Countercurrent\",\r\n      \"status\": \"editorial_source_extraction_not_canonical\",\r\n      \"measurement_type\": \"published_mean_section_width\",\r\n      \"width_metric\": \"mean_cross_section_zero_crossing_span\",\r\n      \"approximate_width_km\": 920,\r\n      \"width_range_km\": null,\r\n      \"range_interpretation\": \"Published approximate mean-field section width; no error interval. Two sections do not supply seasonal or annual extrema.\",\r\n      \"geographic_scope\": \"HS6 at 32 W; source NECC mean section band, not one branch or a whole-current width.\",\r\n      \"section_geometry\": null,\r\n      \"section_orientation\": \"Source cross-section component; not a reconstructed flow-normal section.\",\r\n      \"layer\": \"Altimetry-derived surface geostrophic field; no fixed-depth bounds inferred.\",\r\n      \"time_convention\": \"January 1993-December 2017 mean velocity-profile context; month precision. Not a mean of daily widths or a dated section.\",\r\n      \"boundary_rule\": \"Paired zero contours of the mean signed cross-section velocity; eastward positive. Half-peak intensity domain is a different definition.\",\r\n      \"source_url\": \"https://os.copernicus.